---
import Component from "../../../src/components/volunteer/VolunteerProjectBody.astro";
import "../../../src/styles/tokens.css";

// Isolation page for VolunteerProjectBody — codeyam screenshots the #codeyam-capture
// wrapper by navigating to /isolated-components/VolunteerProjectBody.
//
// Slotted markup mirrors what Astro's `render()` emits for a project's markdown:
// headings, paragraphs, and the long bulleted list Nicole actually wrote. This is
// the capture that proves the `:global` prose rules reach slotted content — the
// one thing scoped styles cannot do on their own.
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Isolated: VolunteerProjectBody</title>
  </head>
  <body style="margin: 0;">
    <div id="codeyam-capture">
      <div class="s-narrow">
        <Component>
          <p>
            For this specific New York event, the volunteer will support the full social
            media promotion cycle, including:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>Develop a social media content plan and posting schedule for before, during, and after the event.</li>
            <li>Write engaging LinkedIn posts that align with Harvard Alumni in Tech's brand, audience, and event goals.</li>
            <li>Create promotional posts announcing the event, speakers, panelists, partners, and key discussion topics.</li>
            <li>Coordinate with featured individuals to confirm their correct LinkedIn profiles and company pages.</li>
            <li>Monitor engagement and respond to or flag relevant comments and questions.</li>
          </ul>
          <h2>After the event</h2>
          <p>
            Repurpose event photos, videos, audio, quotes, and key takeaways into at least
            six additional pieces of content that can be shared throughout the year.
          </p>
        </Component>
      </div>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
